// DictationBridge state-machine pseudocode (Qt5 APIs; all async):
// Holds: QDBusInterface api(BUS, PATH, BUS, persistentSessionBus), id, generation,
//        phase, stopWhenStarted, invalidated. Set api.setTimeout(100000).
// begin(g): guard allowed && phase==idle; snapshot g; phase=starting;
//   watch api.asyncCall("Start") as QDBusPendingReply<qulonglong>.
//   On error: reset and surface a sanitized error, never log speech.
//   On reply: if generation invalidated, asyncCall("Cancel", reply.id).
//             else store id; phase=recording; if stopWhenStarted finish().
// finish(): if starting: stopWhenStarted=true; return.
//   if recording: phase=transcribing;
//     watch api.asyncCall("Stop", QVariant::fromValue<qulonglong>(id))
//       as QDBusPendingReply<QString>.
//     if success && original generation is current && allowed:
//       emit finalText(generation, reply.value());
//     reset, including pending stop flag. No duplicate commit on repeated release.
// invalidate(): bump bridge generation; mark outstanding Start as invalidated;
//   if id exists asyncCall("Cancel", QVariant::fromValue<qulonglong>(id)); reset.
// on StatusChanged(idle,false): reset visible recording state; do not invalidate a
//   pending Stop generation, since idle precedes its successful method reply.
// on service disappearance: invalidate, clear indicator and surface unavailable.
// Watchers deleteLater() on every completion, including errors and stale replies.
// Also call invalidate() from keyboard hide, session lock, input hint changes.
// mayDictate() must reject hidden text, password, PIN, no focus and locked session.
